Subject: WebCore: out-of-line TimingFunction destructors for PS5_HOMEBREW

With clang 18 targeting x86_64-sie-ps5, the vtables of
Linear/Steps/SpringTimingFunction reference their implicit complete
object destructors (D1), but no translation unit emits them, so the
final link fails with undefined WebCore::*TimingFunction::~*(). Declare
the destructors in the header and define them (= default) in
TimingFunction.cpp.
diff --git a/Source/WebCore/platform/animation/TimingFunction.cpp b/Source/WebCore/platform/animation/TimingFunction.cpp
index 2ec1d097e..1ef10ef49 100644
--- a/Source/WebCore/platform/animation/TimingFunction.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebCore/platform/animation/TimingFunction.cpp
@@ -33,6 +33,12 @@
 
 namespace WebCore {
 
+#if defined(PS5_HOMEBREW)
+LinearTimingFunction::~LinearTimingFunction() = default;
+StepsTimingFunction::~StepsTimingFunction() = default;
+SpringTimingFunction::~SpringTimingFunction() = default;
+#endif
+
 TextStream& operator<<(TextStream& ts, const TimingFunction& timingFunction)
 {
     switch (timingFunction.type()) {
